   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The Perfekt tense of the passive",
     "texto": [
      "In order to describe a completed action in the passive voice within standard conversational or commercial register, the periphrasis **conjugated sein in the present + Partizip II of the main verb + worden** is used: **Die Sendung ist gestern zugestellt worden** (the shipment has been delivered yesterday). In this pattern the passive auxiliary werden necessarily takes the reduced participle form **worden** (without the prefix ge-)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Syntactic order and use",
     "texto": [
      "At the end of the main clause two participles accumulate (**Partizip II + worden**), with the conjugated auxiliary **ist / sind** reserved for the second metric position: **Alle Rechnungen sind bereits beglichen worden** (all the invoices have already been settled)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Structure",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "Temporal function",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Example",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
     "filas": [
      [
       {
        "texto": "ist + Partizip II + worden",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "Completed passive process (singular)",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "Das Paket ist verschickt worden.",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "texto": "sind + Partizip II + worden",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "Completed passive process (plural)",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "Die Verträge sind geprüft worden.",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "texto": "war + Partizip II + worden",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "Passive Plusquamperfekt (anteriority)",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "Die Ware war storniert worden.",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       }
      ]
     ],
